    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "German media across the spectrum agree that the war in Ukraine has triggered a “Zeitenwende” for German security policy, prompting a broadly shared call for accelerated defence spending, faster procurement of high‑tech weapon systems and a concrete push to meet NATO’s 2 percent target. At the same time, reports from left, centre and right uniformly highlight internal challenges – notably the need for structural reforms such as the possible re‑introduction of conscription and the overhaul of Bundeswehr culture to curb sexual misconduct and improve cyber‑defence capabilities – as essential preconditions for a credible NATO contribution and effective civil protection.",
